---
import HTML5 from "@cyberfinity/polymorph-components-astro/layouts/HTML5.astro";
import PageHeader from "@cyberfinity/polymorph-components-astro/components/PageHeader.astro";
import PageFooter from "@cyberfinity/polymorph-components-astro/components/PageFooter.astro";
import EveSubSiteWidget from "@cyberfinity/event-horizon-site/components/EveSubSiteWidget.astro";
import { getSubSiteUrl } from "@cyberfinity/astro-helpers";
---

<HTML5 title="Outpost images">
  <Fragment slot="head-content">
    <link rel="icon" href={getSubSiteUrl(Astro.url, "./favicon.ico")} />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      type="text/css"
      href={getSubSiteUrl(Astro.url, "./outpost.css")}
    />
    <link
      rel="meta"
      type="application/rdf+xml"
      href={getSubSiteUrl(Astro.url, "./index.rdf")}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <PageHeader>
    <h1>Outpost pictures</h1>
  </PageHeader>
  <main>
    <p>
      These pictures were designed as backgrounds for the <a
        class="secret"
        href="http://burpmancorp.cyberfinity.net/"
        >Burpman Corporation Productions (<acronym
          title="Burpman Corporation Productions">BCP</acronym
        >)</a
      > &amp; <a class="secret" href="http://mentalmix.cyberfinity.net/"
        >Mental Mix</a
      > Outpost websites, <a href="https://twid.tripod.com/">Outpost 1</a> and <a
        href="https://members.tripod.com/~smoggs_denn/">Outpost 2</a
      >. They are available under a <a href="https://creativecommons.org/"
        >Creative Commons</a
      > license, meaning that you can freely download and re-use them as long as
      you attribute me as the original artist (a link to this page or to <a
        href="https://cirrus.twiddles.com/">my website</a
      > would suffice). Please note that there are some additional restrictions too,
      click the license buttons by the images for the full details.
    </p>
    <p>Enjoy!</p>

    <h2>Mountain Outpost</h2>
    <div>
      <a
        href="mountain_outpost.jpg"
        title="Download full-sized image"
        class="thumbnail"
        ><img
          src="mountain_outpost_thumb.jpg"
          alt="Thumbnail of Mountain Outpost picture (click to download)"
        /></a
      >
    </div>
    <dl>
      <dt>Description:</dt>
      <dd>
        <p>
          Picture of a large, dark watch-tower standing on a snowy mountain
          range surrounded by whispy clouds.
        </p>
      </dd>

      <dt>Source works:</dt>
      <dd>
        <p>
          The clouds in the background are taken from the top half of the photo <a
            href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/moe/285192/in/pool-creativecommons/"
            lang="de">&ldquo;Alter jüdischer Friedhof bei Leihgestern&rdquo;</a
          > by Stephan Mosel. The mountain range is from the photo <a
            href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/pberry/1332680/in/pool-creativecommons/"
            >&ldquo;Panorama from Mt. Lassen Trail&rdquo;</a
          > by Patrick Berry. Both these works are also available under Creative
          Commons licenses.
        </p>
      </dd>

      <dt>Tools used:</dt>
      <dd>
        <a href="https://www.gimp.org/"
          >The <acronym title="GNU Image Manipulation Program">GIMP</acronym></a
        >
      </dd>

      <dt>Size:</dt>
      <dd>
        1600 x 800, 29kb (<acronym title="Joint Photo Experts Group"
          >JPEG</acronym
        > format)
      </dd>

      <dt>License:</dt>
      <dd>
        <a
          rel="license"
          href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/2.5/"
          class="license"
          ><img alt="Creative Commons Logo" src="somerights.gif" /></a
        > This work is licensed under a <a
          rel="license"
          href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/2.5/"
          >Creative Commons License</a
        >.
      </dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Urban Outpost</h2>
    <div>
      <a
        href="urban_outpost.jpg"
        title="Download full-sized image"
        class="thumbnail"
        ><img
          src="urban_outpost_thumb.jpg"
          alt="Thumbnail of Urban Outpost picture (click to download)"
        /></a
      >
    </div>
    <dl>
      <dt>Description:</dt>
      <dd>
        <p>Picture of a machine-like, dark tower against an brewing storm.</p>
      </dd>

      <dt>Source works:</dt>
      <dd>
        <p>
          The tower is a collage of &ldquo;Beaver Stadium 1&rdquo; by
          &ldquo;oceanfrog&rdquo;, <a
            href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/johndan/31428882/"
            >&ldquo;Connected&rdquo;</a
          > by Johndan Johnson-Eilola, &ldquo;Tower&rdquo; by Victor Geere and <a
            href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/remydwd/2988129/"
            >&ldquo;The back of my Xserves&rdquo;</a
          > by Dan Dickinson.
        </p>
        <p>
          The sky is composed of <a
            href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/denn/20450050/"
            >&ldquo;Stormclouds&rdquo;</a
          > by Denise Chan and <a
            href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/mcclanahan/15370959/"
            >&ldquo;Impending&rdquo;</a
          > by Lorrie McClanahan.
        </p>
        <p>All these works are available under Creative Commons licenses.</p>
      </dd>

      <dt>Tools used:</dt>
      <dd>
        <a href="https://www.gimp.org/"
          >The <acronym title="GNU Image Manipulation Program">GIMP</acronym></a
        >
      </dd>
      <dd>
        <a href="https://developer.apple.com/macosx/coreimage.html"
          >Core Image Fun House</a
        >
      </dd>

      <dt>Size:</dt>
      <dd>
        1600 x 1200, 76kb (<acronym title="Joint Photo Experts Group"
          >JPEG</acronym
        > format)
      </dd>

      <dt>License:</dt>
      <dd>
        <a
          rel="license"
          href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.5/"
          class="license"
          ><img alt="Creative Commons Logo" src="somerights.gif" /></a
        > This work is licensed under a <a
          rel="license"
          href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.5/"
          >Creative Commons License</a
        >.
      </dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Leaves</h2>
    <div>
      <a href="leaves.jpg" title="Download full-sized image" class="thumbnail"
        ><img
          src="leaves_thumb.jpg"
          alt="Thumbnail of Leaves picture (click to download)"
        /></a
      >
    </div>
    <dl>
      <dt>Description:</dt>
      <dd>
        <p>
          Pale picture of tree branches with autumn leaves against a clear blue
          sky.
        </p>
      </dd>

      <dt>Source works:</dt>
      <dd>
        <p>
          This picture is based on the photo <a
            href="https://openphoto.net/gallery/image/view/7014"
            >&ldquo;Tree sky&rdquo;</a
          > by Mario Pena, which is also available under a Creative Commons license.
        </p>
      </dd>

      <dt>Tools used:</dt>
      <dd>
        <a href="https://www.gimp.org/"
          >The <acronym title="GNU Image Manipulation Program">GIMP</acronym></a
        >
      </dd>

      <dt>Size:</dt>
      <dd>
        1006 x 851, 37kb (<acronym title="Joint Photo Experts Group"
          >JPEG</acronym
        > format)
      </dd>

      <dt>License:</dt>
      <dd>
        <a
          rel="license"
          href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5/"
          class="license"
          ><img alt="Creative Commons Logo" src="somerights.gif" /></a
        > This work is licensed under a <a
          rel="license"
          href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5/"
          >Creative Commons License</a
        >.
      </dd>
    </dl>

    <p class="clear">
      If you intend to use these pictures as backgrounds for your own website(s)
      or want to embed them in some other way <em>please</em> do not hotlink directly
      to the files hosted here on <a href="/"
        ><acronym title="Event-horizon.Twiddles.Com">ETC</acronym></a
      >. I just don't have the bandwidth to support that! Instead, download the
      pictures you want, upload them to your own webspace and <em>then</em> embed
      them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Of course if you just want to place a normal link to where you got the
      pictures from that's fine (in fact I'd really appreciate it!) - but please
      link to this page rather than directly to the picture file.
    </p>
    <p>Thanks for reading and have fun with the pictures!</p>
    <p class="signature">- James</p>
  </main>
  <PageFooter>
    <p>
      © 2005 <a href="https://cirrus.twiddles.com/">James Nash</a>. <a
        href="index.rdf"
        >Download copyright meta-data as <acronym
          title="Resource Description Framework">RDF</acronym
        ></a
      >.
    </p>
    <EveSubSiteWidget />
  </PageFooter>
</HTML5>
